<title>SPAIN: B.of Spain Rojo says fear of weak euro unjustified.</title>
<headline>B.of Spain Rojo says fear of weak euro unjustified.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Spain governor Luis Angel Rojo said on Wednesday fears of a weak euro, which had partly been responsible for the recent dollar rise, were not justified, local news agency Europa Press reported.</p>
<p>&quot;I do not see these fears as justified,&quot; Rojo was reported saying.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 8340</p>
</text>
